From 7a4c5f021990fc35cb96c8a666fb61276c43c643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zirize <zirize@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:44:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Close the last four gaps in the agent tests

All four were areas only a real game had ever exercised, which is the slowest
place to find out they had broken.

screen_text in 80 columns reads each pair of columns out of two banks - the
even column from auxiliary memory, the odd one from main - and only the
40-column path had ever been checked. The case writes a different pattern into
each bank and asks for the row: with the auxiliary read removed it comes back
as "1122334455" instead of "A1B2C3D4E5".

screen_hires and screen_capture hand back memory as base64 and nothing had
ever decoded it. Both cases decode and compare byte for byte - the hi-res one
against a pattern rather than a constant, so a decoder that dropped or
reordered bytes could not pass, and against page 2 as well to show the page
parameter is honoured.

run_frames turns turbo off to stay reproducible, and turbo belongs to the host
rather than the machine: not putting it back leaves the window running at the
wrong speed afterwards. The case also shows why the run asks for it at all -
the same frames cost the same cycles whether the host was in turbo or not.
Disk turbo is the user's setting in the same way and is checked the same.

And the server holds more than one client: a person watching a session while a
tool drives it is two connections. Each gets its own reply, told apart by the
id it sent, and one leaving does not disturb the other.

40 cases. The slot 0 cases that sent colliding ids are gone: the command
subsystems ended the sharing, and upstream's test_slot0_dispatch.cpp covers
slot 0 now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
